# REGEX-PCRE2-FIDELITY.3.1 (PGEN-REGEX-PCRE2-0007): MAX_FALSE_REJECT_TOTAL corrected 45 -> 46.
# This +1 is PRE-EXISTING drift, NOT introduced by .3.1. A stash-baseline measurement (the parser
# regenerated with the .3.1 grammar + validator changes reverted) produced an IDENTICAL 46-element
# false-reject set (same case IDs; false_accept=292, mismatch=338 also unchanged) — proving the .3.1
# escape catch-all restructure + find_invalid_escape_i migration are EXACTLY conformance-neutral on the
# PCRE2 compile oracle. The prior env (v9, =45) was stale vs the current corpus (2195 cases, unchanged).
# All 46 false rejects are documented strict-default divergence classes (empty `[]`, \K-in-lookaround,
# alt_bsux \u, class-set operations, extended `(?[...])`, MARK/verb edge cases) that the default (pcre2)
# profile intentionally does not accept; several are tracked for future leaves (.3.7 empty-`[]`,
# row #10 \K-in-lookaround).
# REGEX-PCRE2-FIDELITY.3.18 (PGEN-REGEX-PCRE2-0016): baseline v11. Two changes, both slice-verified:
# (1) the counted-quantifier brace model moved into the grammar (quant_bound_number + the
# literal_open_brace guard), flipping 4 corpus accepts-invalid cells to correct rejects
# (false_accept 292 -> 288, match 1857 -> 1860 on the v10 universe); (2) the normalizer now skips the
# `expand` suffix modifier (6 cells: 2195 -> 2189 cases, ok 1613 -> 1609, fail 582 -> 580) because
# pcre2test macro-expands `\[...]{n}` BEFORE compiling, so pairing the raw line text with the observed
# verdict is unsound by construction — testinput2's `/\[AB]{6000000000000000000000}/expand` ingested as
# expected=ok while its raw text is a plain err-105 reject; post-grammar-fix PGEN correctly rejects it
# and the cell mis-counted as a false reject (47 vs the true 46). The false-reject ratchet stays EXACT
# at 46: the same documented strict-default divergence classes as v10 (empty `[]`, \K-in-lookaround,
# alt_bsux \u, class-set operations, extended `(?[...])`, MARK/verb edge cases).
# REGEX-PCRE2-FIDELITY.3.21 (PGEN-REGEX-PCRE2-0019): the LIMIT `=value` range bound moved into the
# grammar ([0, 4294967289] on directive_payload_digits, ledger REGEX-0097). EXACTLY byte-identical on
# this corpus — decisive stash-baseline (grammar reverted + parser regen): OLD == NEW at match=1858,
# false_accept=285, false_reject=46, mismatch=331 over 2189 cases (zero corpus cells flipped — every
# corpus `LIMIT=value` is in-range: =0/=123/=1). RECORD CORRECTION: the true measured baseline is
# 1858/285/46, not the 1857/286/46 carried in MEMORY/leaf notes since .3.18 — a .3.18 universe-shift
# bookkeeping artifact propagated by the .3.19/.3.20 "byte-identical" assertions without re-measurement.
# The ratchet thresholds below (MIN_MATCH=1845, MAX_FALSE_ACCEPT=299, MAX_FALSE_REJECT=46) are
# unaffected and stay as-is; the false-reject set is the same documented 46 strict-default divergences.
PGEN_REGEX_PCRE2_COMPILE_ORACLE_BASELINE_VERSION=11
PGEN_REGEX_PCRE2_COMPILE_ORACLE_REF=pcre2-10.47
PGEN_REGEX_PCRE2_COMPILE_ORACLE_EXPECTED_CASES=2189
PGEN_REGEX_PCRE2_COMPILE_ORACLE_EXPECTED_PARSE_OK_TOTAL=1609
PGEN_REGEX_PCRE2_COMPILE_ORACLE_EXPECTED_PARSE_FAIL_TOTAL=580
PGEN_REGEX_PCRE2_COMPILE_ORACLE_MIN_MATCH_TOTAL=1845
PGEN_REGEX_PCRE2_COMPILE_ORACLE_MAX_MISMATCH_TOTAL=344
PGEN_REGEX_PCRE2_COMPILE_ORACLE_MAX_FALSE_ACCEPT_TOTAL=299
PGEN_REGEX_PCRE2_COMPILE_ORACLE_MAX_FALSE_REJECT_TOTAL=46
